--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -17,3 +17,11 @@ An order takes at most one discount code, set with `applyCode(orderNumber, code)
 An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused with an error and the order is left as it was. The
 discount never touches shipping, and free shipping is decided on the items before any discount. `totals` shows
 `discountCents` (0 without a code); `totalCents` is items minus discount plus shipping.
+
+## Monthly export
+
+`exportMonth(month)` gives the accountant's export of a month (`YYYY-MM`) as CSV text: a header line, then one line
+per order placed in that month, by order number. Columns: `order`, `date` (as stored), `customer` (the name) and `total` (what the customer pays, discount and shipping included, in euros with two decimals, such as `12.50`).
+The customers' email addresses and phone numbers are deliberately not exported.
+A value with a comma, a quote or a line break is quoted, with quotes doubled. Lines end with `\n`, the last without.
+A month with no orders gives the header line alone; a month that is not `YYYY-MM` throws a `RangeError`.
