+
+# Monthly order export for the accountant
+
+The accountant loads a monthly export of the orders into her spreadsheet.
+
+- API: `OrderBook.exportMonth(month)`, `month` as `YYYY-MM`; returns CSV text.
+- A header line, then one line per order placed in that month, by order number.
+- Columns, in order: `order` (number), `date` (as stored), `customer` (name) and
+  `total` (what the customer pays: `totalCents` with discount and shipping, in euros with two decimals, e.g. `12.50`).
+- Rework after rejection by Dana Okafor: the export must not carry customers' email addresses or phone numbers, so
+  they are not columns.
+- A value containing a comma or a quote (or a line break) is quoted, quotes doubled.
+- A month with no orders gives the header line alone; a malformed month is refused with a `RangeError`.
+- Lines are separated by `\n`, no trailing newline.
+- She wants the first export at the end of this month (October 2026), so this is to be released after approval.
